☎️ 1. When HR calls you
------------------------------
HR: Hello, am I speaking with Rohit?
You: “Yes, this is Rohit speaking.”

If you don't recognize the number:
“Yes, this is Rohit speaking. May I know who’s calling, please?”

If they introduce themselves:
“Thank you for reaching out. How can I help you?”

☎️ 2. HR says: "We found your profile..."
-----------------------------------------------
HR: We found your profile on LinkedIn/Naukri and would like to discuss an opportunity.

You: “Sure, thank you for reaching out. I’d be happy to discuss the opportunity.”

Then listen carefully.
Don't immediately start explaining everything about yourself.

📅 3. Interview Scheduling
-----------------------------------
This is one of the most important situations.

HR: Are you available for an interview tomorrow at 11 AM?

If you're available:
“Yes, I’m available tomorrow at 11 AM. That works for me.”

Or more professionally:
“Yes, tomorrow at 11 AM works well for me. Could you please share the interview details with me?”


📅 4. If HR gives you a time but you didn't hear it clearly
  ----------------------------------------------------------
Don't guess.

Say: “Sorry, could you please repeat the interview time?”

Or:

“I’m sorry, I didn’t catch the time. Could you please repeat it?”

Very useful sentence:
  “I didn’t catch that.”

Example:
“Sorry, I didn’t catch the date. Could you please repeat it?”


📧 5. Ask HR to send details
-------------------------------
After scheduling:
  “Could you please share the interview details over email?”

Or:

“Could you please send me the interview invite and details over email?”

You can also confirm:
“Just to confirm, the interview is scheduled for tomorrow at 11 AM, correct?”

This is very good professional communication.

💻 6. Ask whether it's online or offline
------------------------------------------
“Could you please confirm whether the interview will be conducted online or in person?”

If online:
“Could you please share the meeting link and interview details with me?”

If offline:
“Could you please share the office address and any instructions I need to follow?”

🔄 7. If HR asks: "Can you join the interview immediately?"
---------------------------------------------------------------
If yes:
“Yes, I’m available. I can join immediately.”

If you need some time:
“I’m available today, but I would need some time to prepare. Would 4 PM work for you?”

📞 8. If HR calls when you're busy
-------------------------------------
Don't panic.

Say:
“Thank you for calling. I’m currently unavailable. Would it be possible to speak in about 30 minutes?”

Or:
“I’m sorry, I’m currently in another meeting. Could we connect after 5 PM?”

Don't say:
❌ “I'm busy. Call later.”

📱 9. If you miss HR's call
--------------------------------
Call back if appropriate.

Say:
“Hello, this is Rohit. I noticed I had a missed call from this number. May I know if you were trying to reach me regarding an interview opportunity?”

Excellent sentence to memorize.

🔊 10. If the network is bad
---------------------------------
Very important for phone interviews.

Don't keep saying:
❌ “Hello? Hello? Hello?”

Instead:
“I’m sorry, the connection seems to be a little unclear. Could you please repeat that?”

If it continues:
“I’m sorry, I’m having some network issues. Would it be okay if we reconnect in a few minutes?”


16. At the end HR says: "Do you have any questions?"
--------------------------------------------------------
Never feel that you must say "No."

Ask one or two useful questions.

Good question #1
“Could you please tell me a little about the interview process and the next steps?”

Good question #2
“Could you please share the technology stack for this role?”

Good question #3
“Could you please let me know what I should prepare for the technical interview?”

These are excellent for a fresher/early-career candidate.

